silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegMeasuresExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_3 silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegMeasures', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 plus the Set-enrichment of O_01: Hom_O_01(Measurement2024, Mittens) = {measures}. The 2024-11-01 body-mass measurement (4.1kg) measures the cat Mittens; the typed hom-set is small and named. The Set-enrichment guarantees that adding \"measured at a vet visit\" as a second arrow would require an explicit olog extension, not a fluent assumption." .
